A||||5||Ed||Door ajar switch||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||07-26-2001||09:54 PM||||What does it take to replace the door ajar switch at the door latch?<P>Doesn't seem accessible from the inner door panel.<P>I may just take out the instrument panel "door ajar" light if its too big a deal.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||07-26-2001||10:11 PM||||All I can remember is that it is no fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  When I put 85 power doors on my 87 coupe, I removed the switches from my original 87 doors and put them into the 85 doors so that I retained the Door Ajar function.  If I remember correctly I did most of the work from the outside of the door while the outer panels were off.  It's just another one of those jobs that you need long fingers and small hands and lots of patience for.  I think there is only one screw that holds the switch in but it was a bear to get the switch into the proper position...  Have fun!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||07-27-2001||09:48 AM||||DOOR AJAR switches are available at your friendly Pontiac dealer and are very easy to change.  I just change out the driver's door switch.  Pull out the carpet at the switch and the wire is easy to access.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||07-27-2001||11:22 AM||||I think Ed is talking about the ajar switch that is located inside the door itself, attached to the door latch mechanism on the later years Fieros.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ed||07-27-2001||11:48 AM||||Yep, the one buried inside the dark recesses of the inner door panel, built into the latch mechanism.  ('87)<P>Any consequences besides the obvious in pulling the lamp?  Wiring diagram doesn't show it connected to any other circuits. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||07-27-2001||11:52 AM||||None that I know of but if you want a switch, I have one.  All I have to do is pull it out of the door since I currently have both the inner and outer panels off.  I don't need it because the 85 I have put the door on has a different type of ajar switch. Let me know....||||reg||1
